+{"v":1,"seq":324,"channel":"control","type":"message.final","session_id":"replay_session","turn_id":"fixture-turn-1","message_id":"msg_095ba2c797e2c76d0169815d8af45c81a0ad58a406137aee54","content":"This repo is for **ctx**, an Agentic Development Environment (ADE) that runs a local daemon to orchestrate coding agents across real workspaces. It’s a vendor‑neutral control plane for tasks/sessions/runs, ctx Packs (specs/skills/prompts), and multi‑agent workflows, with clients including a desktop app (Tauri web workbench), experimental desktop UI client, and mobile apps. The daemon owns state (workspaces, worktrees, tasks, sessions, runs, events) and exposes a local HTTP/WebSocket API; agents are integrated via provider adapters (Codex, Claude, Gemini, etc.), and large payloads stream via a data plane (artifacts, PTY, WebRTC).  \n\nIf you want, I can point you to the most relevant top‑level docs or walk through the main folders (`core/`, `harness-adapters/`, `external-harnesses/`, `docs/`, `supabase/`)."}
